  "changelog": "Initial release of D-InSAR coherence and phase analysis skill.\n\n- Estimates complex coherence and interferometric phase from registered master/slave SLC input, supporting both real and synthetic data.\n- Supports flexible multi-looking window size via `--looks-r` and `--looks-a`.\n- Outputs GeoTIFF files for coherence and phase, with statistics and run manifest in JSON.\n- Offers command line interface with examples for various scenarios (real data, synthetic, polarization selection, low-coherence threshold).\n- Fully offline processing; all data stays local.\n- Includes documentation in both English and Chinese.",
